.dart_tool/
build/

# Drift generates this. A fresh clone needs
# `dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs` before it compiles.
*.g.dart

# ── Signing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE KEYSTORE AND ITS PASSWORDS NEVER GO IN THE REPOSITORY.
#
# This repository IS public — it lives inside nuno927-tech/stash-it alongside
# the web app — so a mistake here is published the moment it is pushed, and
# GitHub keeps it in the history even after it is deleted.
#
# But the rule would stand either way, because the upload key is the one secret
# in this project that cannot be rotated. Lose it and the app on the Play Store
# can never be updated again by anybody, including you; leak it and somebody
# else can publish an update that Android will install over the real one
# without a warning.
#
# Back it up somewhere that is not this folder and not this laptop. See
# RELEASE.md.
*.jks
*.keystore
android/key.properties

# ── Editor state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These were tracked for the first sixty versions, which nobody noticed while
# the repository was a folder on one laptop. They are worth removing now for
# three reasons, in ascending order of importance:
#
#   They are noise. `.vs/` alone was 1.4 MB of binary index and symbol
#   databases that changed on every build, so every commit carried a diff
#   nobody wrote.
#
#   They are machine-specific. `.idea/libraries/Dart_SDK.xml` names the
#   absolute path of one Flutter install; anybody cloning this gets a broken
#   project configuration rather than none.
#
#   They are not reviewable. A `.wsuo` or a `.sqlite` cannot be read in a
#   diff, so nobody can tell what is in one — which is exactly the sort of
#   file that ends up carrying a token or a local path nobody meant to share.
.idea/
.vs/
*.iml
*.iws

# Points at wherever Flutter is installed on this machine.
android/local.properties

# One-time utility for moving this project into the web repository. Not part
# of the project, and meaningless once it has run.
merge-into-monorepo.ps1
